| $9$ |  |  |" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8y+6x-3z+4 &=0 \\\\ 5z-3y+x-6 &=0 \\\\ 7x-4z-y-9 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$8$</td><td>$-3$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>$-3$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$-1$</td><td>$-4$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$z$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$9$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">.</span>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186605132 :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2z &=4y-1 \\\\ x+2 &=y-z \\\\ y &=1+x+2z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2z &=4y-1 \\\\ x+2 &=y-z \\\\ y &=1+x+2z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$x=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186612436 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3z-6x-4 &=0 \\\\ 2y-x-3z-1 &=0 \\\\ 5y+2x-9 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-6$ | {{field-1}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-1$ | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $1$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $5$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3z-6x-4 &=0 \\\\ 2y-x-3z-1 &=0 \\\\ 5y+2x-9 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-6$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$3$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$5$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$z$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">.</span>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186612448 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+2x+y-1 &=0 \\\\ y+2z+3x &=2 \\\\ x+5z+2y-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | $2$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+2x+y-1 &=0 \\\\ y+2z+3x &=2 \\\\ x+5z+2y-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$1$</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$z$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">.</span>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186647103 :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\nfind $AB.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$AB=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\nfind $AB.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186059953 :question/worked-solution nil "Rearrange the equations so that each left side lists the coefficients of $x,y,z$ in that order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z&=-1\\\\4y+5z&=0\\\\x+6z&=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMatching the indicated entries gives $a=0$, $b=5$, and $c=-1$."] [:db/cas 17592186060277 :question/worked-solution nil "Each row of the coefficient matrix lists the coefficients of $x,y,z$ in the corresponding equation. The missing entries are the coefficient $5$ of $z$ in the first equation, the coefficient $8$ of $z$ in the second equation, and the coefficient $0$ of $x$ in the third equation. Thus $a=5$, $b=8$, and $c=0$."] [:db/cas 17592186060278 :question/worked-solution nil "The matrix is diagonal, so its determinant is the product of its diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n2\\cdot7\\cdot(-3)=-42.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186060451 :question/worked-solution nil "The first equation is $1x+0y+0z=6$. The third equation rearranges to $-2x+0y+3z=2$. Matching these coefficients and constants with the matrix representation gives $a=1$, $b=0$, and $c=2$."] [:db/cas 17592186060455 :question/worked-solution nil "Expanding across the first row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}0&-1&3\\\\2&0&1\\\\7&-1&0\\end{vmatrix}&=0-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}2&1\\\\7&0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}2&0\\\\7&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=(-7)+3(-2)\\\\&=-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186088366 :question/worked-solution nil "Multiplying $A$ and $C$ in both orders gives\n\n$$\nAC=CA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}=I_2.\n$$\n\nThus $C=A^{-1}$. Since $B\\ne C$, statement III is false. Also\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1&1\\\\-2&0\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I_2,\n$$\n\nso statement I is false. Only statement II is true."] [:db/cas 17592186092817 :question/worked-solution nil "The constant vector is $b=\\begin{bmatrix}7\\\\-1\\\\-5\\end{bmatrix}$. Multiplying by the given inverse gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{bmatrix}=A^{-1}b=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0&2\\\\2&-2&3\\\\1&-1&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7\\\\-1\\\\-5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\1\\\\3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore $x+y+z=-3+1+3=1$."] [:db/cas 17592186101102 :question/worked-solution nil "Here, $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $Y$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $XY$ is $2\\times 3$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{2}}}}{X}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{2}}}\\times3}{Y}=\\underset{2\\times3}{XY}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $1$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{0} & \\ast & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $2$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\boxed{1} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{13}$, use row $1$ of $X$ (blue) and column $3$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & \\boxed{14} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{13}&={\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $X$ (blue) and column $1$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ \\boxed{1} & \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-1}}) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $X$ (blue) and column $2$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{red}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{0} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{0}} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{23}$, use row $2$ of $X$ (blue) and column $3$ of $Y$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{red}{2}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{-1}} & {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{red}{4}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\boxed{-4}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{23}&={\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{2}}+({\\color{#4169E1}{-1}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{4}} \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nXY=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101103 :question/worked-solution nil "The product of a $3\\times1$ matrix and a $1\\times2$ matrix is a $3\\times2$ matrix. Multiply each entry of the column by each entry of the row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2&4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\cdot2&3\\cdot4\\\\0\\cdot2&0\\cdot4\\\\1\\cdot2&1\\cdot4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6&12\\\\0&0\\\\2&4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101104 :question/worked-solution nil "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. The matching inner dimensions show that the product is defined, and $AB$ is $2\\times 2$:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2\\times\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}}{A}\\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}{\\checkmark}}}{\\cdot}\\underset{\\boxed{{\\color{#2E8B57}{3}}}\\times2}{B}=\\underset{2\\times2}{AB}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{11}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{5}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{6}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{9}} & {\\color{gray}{8}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{7}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}\\boxed{48} & \\ast \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11}&={\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{6}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{9}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ &=48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{12}$, use row $1$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{#4169E1}{5}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{0}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{-2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{6}} & {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{9}} & {\\color{red}{8}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{7}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & \\boxed{54} \\\\ \\ast & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{12}&={\\color{#4169E1}{5}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{8}} \\\\ &\\quad +{\\color{#4169E1}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{7}} \\\\ &=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{21}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $1$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{5}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{6}} & {\\color{gray}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{9}} & {\\color{gray}{8}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{3}} & {\\color{gray}{7}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 54 \\\\ \\boxed{3} & \\ast\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21}&={\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{6}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{9}} \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor entry $c_{22}$, use row $2$ of $A$ (blue) and column $2$ of $B$ (red):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{5}} & {\\color{gray}{1}} & {\\color{gray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{#4169E1}{0}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{1}} & {\\color{#4169E1}{-2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}{6}} & {\\color{red}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{9}} & {\\color{red}{8}} \\\\ {\\color{gray}{3}} & {\\color{red}{7}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 54 \\\\ 3 & \\boxed{-6}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{22}&={\\color{#4169E1}{0}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{5}}+{\\color{#4169E1}{1}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{8}} \\\\ &\\quad +({\\color{#4169E1}{-2}})\\cdot {\\color{red}{7}} \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 54 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101140 :question/worked-solution nil "The matrix $C$ has size $1\\times2$, while $D$ has size $3\\times1$. The number of columns in $C$ is $2$, and the number of rows in $D$ is $3$. These inner dimensions differ, so $CD$ is undefined."] [:db/cas 17592186101529 :question/worked-solution nil "Multiply row $1$ of $A$ by column $3$ of $B$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{13}&=\\begin{bmatrix}-1&2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=(-1)(-2)+2(5)\\\\&=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101530 :question/worked-solution nil "Multiply row $4$ of $X$ by column $2$ of $Y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z_{42}&=\\begin{bmatrix}-5&6&-2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=(-5)(-3)+6(0)+(-2)(1)\\\\&=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186106290 :question/worked-solution nil "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1&0&2&2\\\\0&1&-3&1\\\\2&0&-4&-4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nApply $R_1:=-R_1$ and then $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$. This gives the row echelon form\n\n$$\nM\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&0&-2&-2\\\\0&1&-3&1\\\\0&0&0&0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186115742 :question/worked-solution nil "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}$. Then\n\n$$\nEA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&-2\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a-2c&b-2d\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe second row is unchanged, and the first row becomes the first row minus twice the second row. Therefore the operation is $R_1:=R_1+(-2)R_2$."] [:db/cas 17592186115751 :question/worked-solution nil "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&1&2&19\\\\3&1&2&31\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nApply $R_2:=R_2-3R_1$, then $R_2:=-\\frac12R_2$, and finally $R_1:=R_1-R_2$. The reduced row echelon form is\n\n$$\nM\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&0&0&6\\\\0&1&2&13\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nHence $x=6$ and $y=13-2z$, with $z$ free. The solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6\\\\13-2z\\\\z\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186115844 :question/worked-solution nil "The operation $R_1:=R_1-5R_2$ corresponds to left multiplication by $E_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1&-5\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}$. The operation $R_1:=3R_1$ corresponds to left multiplication by $E_2=\\begin{bmatrix}3&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}$. Because $E_1$ acts first, the required product is\n\n$$\nE_2E_1A=\\begin{bmatrix}3&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1&-5\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}A.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186115845 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the row operation to the identity matrix to obtain the elementary matrix\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac14&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding operation on $A$ is left multiplication:\n\n$$\nEA=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac14&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}A.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186115846 :question/worked-solution nil "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}$. Then\n\n$$\nEA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\7&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\7a+c&7b+d\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe first row is unchanged, and the second row becomes the second row plus seven times the first row. Therefore the operation is $R_2:=R_2+7R_1$."] [:db/cas 17592186120434 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply $R_1:=R_1+2R_4$, $R_2:=R_2+R_4$, and $R_3:=R_3-2R_4$. Adding a multiple of one row to another does not change the determinant, so it becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}5&0&1&-4\\\\-7&0&-2&2\\\\-11&0&-5&3\\\\2&1&4&-7\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpanding down column $2$, the only nonzero entry is $a_{42}=1$. Its cofactor sign is $(-1)^{4+2}=1$. Therefore the original determinant equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}5&1&-4\\\\-7&-2&2\\\\-11&-5&3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186120450 :question/worked-solution nil "The determinant of a product equals the product of the determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A)&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt3&-4\\\\-1&5\\sqrt3\\end{vmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}7&2\\\\5&3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=(15-4)(21-10)\\\\&=11\\cdot11\\\\&=121.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184765 :question/worked-solution nil "First compute\n\n$$\nB^2=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-6&-2+3\\\\12-18&-6+9\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}=B.\n$$\n\nThus $B$ is idempotent, so every positive integer power equals $B$. In particular,\n\n$$\nB^5=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186056077 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186056082] [:db/cas 17592186058284 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186058286] [:db/cas 17592186058290 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186058292] [:db/cas 17592186059328 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186059333] [:db/cas 17592186059352 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186059354] [:db/cas 17592186086849 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186086851] [:db/cas 17592186091102 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186091107] [:db/cas 17592186097947 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186097952] [:db/cas 17592186097953 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186097958] [:db/cas 17592186097959 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186097962] [:db/cas 17592186098175 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186098176] [:db/cas 17592186100335 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186100340] [:db/cas 17592186100341 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186100346] [:db/cas 17592186102770 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186102772] [:db/cas 17592186103888 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186103889] [:db/cas 17592186113418 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186113420] [:db/cas 17592186113472 :answer-field/correct nil 17592186113476] [:db/cas 17592186114001